  "$comment": "Mission 1.26 reference labels for the SAME_PROBLEM_FAMILY relation.\n\nNOT HUMAN GROUND TRUTH, AND NOT THE HUMAN_OPERATOR SET. These 40 labels were produced by GPT-5.6 Sol after reviewing the blind batch and attempting to follow the operator's demonstrated decisions from Mission 1.25. They are AI_ASSISTED_PROVISIONAL, and the repository must never describe them as HUMAN_OPERATOR, human ground truth, expert labels, or independently human-reviewed labels.\n\nTHE OPERATOR CHOSE TO PROCEED USING THEM. That is a project decision about how to spend attention, and it changes nothing about what the labels are: `human_ground_truth_established` is false, and it is recorded in `operator_decision` at document level rather than as a field on a label, because the schema needs no new column to hold a decision about a whole file.\n\nMISSION 1.25's HUMAN HOLDOUT IS A DIFFERENT THING AND STAYS ONE. Its 10 pairs are genuinely HUMAN_OPERATOR, they are not merged into this set, and merging them to satisfy a composition threshold here is exactly what must not happen.\n\nWHAT THEY WERE WRITTEN AGAINST. The blind batch: no model had seen any pair under this rubric, no prediction existed, and no model output entered the sampling that chose them. That makes them a usable provisional reference for exploratory DEVELOPMENT work. It does not make them validated holdout evidence.\n\nNo Stack Overflow author identity appears anywhere -- none was ever acquired.",
